    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Windows at 100%: 7 now, 0 before (+7 windows).",
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Unused quota at reset: 40 now, 74.6154 before (-34.62 percent).",
    },
    {
      "kind": "h2",
      "text": "Suggested changes",
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "7 window(s) reached 100%. Check the forecast earlier in those windows to see the margin before a limit. (Estimated, based on quota_risk_events, forecast_accuracy.)",
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Add a calibration to see how much quota movement your local activity explains. (Estimated, based on attributable_activity.)",
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Enter your plan history and a price to see the prorated plan cost for the week. (Estimated, based on subscription_cost.)",
    },
    {
      "kind": "h2",
      "text": "Definitions",
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Provider mix (provider_mix): Share of locally counted requests per provider in the period. Requests are counted from local logs only. Excludes activity on other devices without a collector and activity that never reached a local log.",
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Supported-client mix (client_mix): Share of locally counted requests per supported client (web, Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, desktop, API). Unattributed records are reported separately and never assigned to a client.",
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Quota risk events (quota_risk_events): Number of quota windows in the period whose provider-reported usage reached the risk threshold (default 80%), and how many reached 100%. Counts windows, not minutes. A window with no snapshot near its peak can be undercounted.",
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Prevented interruptions (prevented_interruptions): Number of times the user confirmed that an alert or Autopilot suggestion let them avoid hitting a limit. Never inferred from alerts or forecasts. Without a confirmation the value is unavailable, not zero. Needs your input.",
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Reset utilization (reset_utilization): Mean of the last provider-reported usage percent in each window that reset during the period. A lower bound: the last snapshot before a reset can precede the true final usage.",
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Unused quota (unused_quota): Mean of 100 minus reset utilization across windows that reset during the period. An upper bound, for the same reason as reset utilization. It is a share of a window, not tokens or money.",
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Forecast accuracy (forecast_accuracy): Mean absolute error, in quota points, of one-hour-ahead forecasts replayed against later snapshots in the period. Shown only with at least 20 comparisons. It describes this account and period, not the model in general.",
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Attributable activity (attributable_activity): Share of provider-reported quota movement that local evidence explains, as a range, with the remainder labelled unattributed. Requires a configured calibration. Without one the value is unavailable.",
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Subscription cost (subscription_cost): Plan price from the pricing catalog (or a manual override), prorated to the days each plan was active in the period, per currency. The plan history is entered by the user. Currencies are never converted or added together. No savings are derived from tokens. Needs your input.",
    },
  ],
  "newUser": false,
  "notices": [],
  "suggestions": [
    "review_limit_windows",
    "add_calibration",
    "add_plan_history",
  ],
}
`;

